  "final_resolution": "### Single Most Important Trade-Off:\nThe single most important trade-off is between the **initial upfront cost and ongoing efficiency**. Building a custom CRM in-house involves a significant initial investment but ensures a tailored solution that can eliminate the need for manual workarounds, thereby enhancing productivity and reducing potential data inconsistencies. On the other hand, buying a SaaS CRM is more cost-effective in the short term but may require additional manual processes and ongoing subscription costs.\n\n### Recommendation:\nBased on the detailed analysis, the **BUY** option is recommended for a 15-person team. While the initial cost of a custom CRM is substantial, the ongoing inefficiencies and potential data inconsistencies from manual workarounds in a SaaS CRM can lead to higher long-term costs and reduced productivity. The SaaS CRM, with its lower upfront cost and flexible pricing options, offers a more balanced solution that is easier to implement and maintain, making it a cost-effective choice for a 15-person team over a 3-year period.",
